  "review_notes": [
    "For the idiomatic Hebrew progression, this alignment assigns the first English 'louder' to הוֹלֵךְ, 'and' to the waw, and the second 'louder' jointly to חָזֵק מְאֹד. Fusing the whole progression is a broader competing analysis, rejected because the first 'louder' and 'and' remain independently meaningful."
